immutable_evidence:
  - The ExactFlat sealed baseline passed only its bounded numerical, controlled-memory, and registered process-crash gates. It is not semantic-memory or product evidence.
  - The frozen TurboVec 0.9.0 four-bit native reference arm is terminally unqualified. Never rerun it, alter its thresholds, or repair its failed process into a pass.
  - Any future compressed-vector arm requires a new preregistration and append-only partial child-process evidence before nonzero-exit rejection.
  - No local fixture, public contract document, or report satisfies authorized MemoryEndpoints individual-account continuity.
engineering_rules:
  - TinyRustLM is pre-release; incur no technical debt and provide no legacy or backward-compatibility support.
  - Rewrite cleanly, remove superseded implementation after verification, and preserve immutable receipts as audit evidence only.
  - Preserve raw failures, fixed seeds, exact identities, bounded allocations, untouched model outputs, and explicit external blockers.
  - Keep static model weights, online KV cache state, durable retrieval vectors, composition graphs, and specialist overlays as separate identity and byte-accounting domains.
  - Do not weaken tests, fabricate live evidence, infer publication from package creation, or infer public reachability from local probes.
  - Keep marketing, documentation, version, release date, last-publish metadata, and per-site update logs synchronized with every stable publication.
next_steps:
  - Validate the committed bounded browser result against the private create-only receipt, run focused JSON/docs/UAI/source-identity gates, commit, push, and prove local HEAD, tracking ref, FETCH_HEAD, and fresh remote are exact.
  - Preregister Template2 before comparative output. Bind exact source-template bytes and revision, accepted Tokenizer2 identity, parser and renderer source closure, role/turn/special-token/whitespace/generation-prompt semantics, bounds, deterministic vectors, independent oracle, output paths, and one verifier invocation.
  - Implement and test Template2 without executing publisher code or adding a Jinja runtime, compatibility reader, repair, or fallback. Preserve any mismatch and use a new append-only registration after a general source fix.
  - Treat missing genuine holdout authors or curriculum reviewers as explicit external blockers; continue only independent engineering work that cannot forge or weaken those gates.
  - Validate every received contribution against the exact current profile, program, identity, custody, order, factor-diversity, overlap, and bounded-storage contracts before assembly.
  - Materialize and review the curriculum without exposing private records in Git or public receipts, then run all contamination controls and preserve every rejection and tombstone.
  - Verify the exact training lock and run the pinned trainer only after `training_authority` is explicitly granted by the current control program.
  - Preserve raw outputs and exact identities through merge, untouched screen, SLM2 conversion, scalar/WASM parity, acquisition, clean-profile browser conversation, privacy scan, and receipts.
  - Run focused tests after each change and complete affected release gates before deployment; commit and push every coherent green major change immediately.
success_criteria:
  - One cryptographically identified derivative has acceptable provenance and passes the preregistered untouched behavioral screen without repair, retry selection, best-of-N, or answer injection.
  - Its exact source, tokenizer, chat template, training data and reviews, adapter, merged bytes, converter, SLM2 output, runtime, WASM, acquisition, and browser receipts form one content-addressed evidence graph.
  - Conversion is deterministic and produces only canonical SLM2; unsupported or ambiguous tensors fail closed and no SLM1 reader, compatibility alias, migration, repair, or fallback exists.
  - Scalar native inference is the reference and browser WASM conforms for identical model bytes, prompts, tokens, sampling profiles, seeds, KV-cache state, stop conditions, and bounded malformed inputs.
  - The browser acquires a verified P2P artifact when available or performs explicit local conversion when unavailable; it never downloads text or scripts as a substitute.
  - A fresh browser profile completes genuine multi-turn local chat with one rendering per answer, truthful cancellation/restart behavior, no prompt or model upload, and deletion/privacy evidence.
  - Complete affected tests pass, source and UAI memory are committed and pushed, documentation and release history are synchronized, deployment occurs only after full gates, and no campaign claim exceeds live receipts.
